    "created_at": "2016-04-25T05:21:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-25T05:22:29Z",
    "body": "In HTML [decode](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#decode)  is used only by [HTM parser](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#the-input-byte-stream:encoding-sniffing-algorithm) and when [fetching script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#fetch-a-classic-script). In first case BOM should correct document's encoding, but for script I don't know if BOM affects any properties or slots.\nBasically you can just correct [this prose](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#determining-the-character-encoding:document%27s-character-encoding-3) to be more clear, add \"Also when decode change encoding (due to BOM) then...\".\n\nDecode is also used in XHR ([text response](https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#text-response)) and once again I don't know if BOM affects any properties or slots. But more interesting is [document response](https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#document-response), I wondering if BOM has any effect, must find some test.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
